<</Type/Annot/Subtype/Highlight/C[.411765 .690196 .945098]/P 13 0 R/F 4/QuadPoints[173.42 297.40437 291.1273 297.40437 173.42 286.3786 291.1273 286.3786 45.36 285.8844 291.22026 285.8844 45.36 274.85865 291.22026 274.85865 45.36 274.48439 291.04338 274.48439 45.36 263.45863 291.04338 263.45863 45.36 262.96443 291.219 262.96443 45.36 251.93866 291.219 251.93866 45.36 251.4444 291.26353 251.4444 45.36 240.41864 291.26353 240.41864 45.36 239.92438 291.0533 239.92438 45.36 228.89862 291.0533 228.89862 45.36 228.37439 291.25999 228.37439 45.36 217.34864 291.25999 217.34864 45.36 216.85437 152.51001 216.85437 45.36 205.82862 152.51001 205.82862]/Rect[42.76112 205.1395 293.8624 298.09349]/AP<</N 371 0 R>>/NM(fitz-A9)/Contents(Deployment and radial control means: spring release, rails, and tether tension\n\nThe platform cover is held in place by a string until reaching the launch point, at which point the cover opens, and the launch mechanism engages, creating tension in the spring and releasing the PocketQube. The rails ensure a smooth exit for the PocketQube, and the tether is gradually released to maintain tension in accordance with the tether calculations, thus keeping the PocketQube at a stable distance from the CubeSat.)/T(CUBICS camera literature review)/Subj(Deployment and radial control means: spring release, rails, and tether tension)/BM/Multiply>>
endobj

