374 0 obj
<</Type/Annot/Subtype/Highlight/C[.411765 .690196 .945098]/P 13 0 R/F 4/QuadPoints[321.07 335.56437 552.42337 335.56437 321.07 324.53865 552.42337 324.53865 306.65 324.04438 552.2238 324.04438 306.65 313.01863 552.2238 313.01863 306.65 312.52436 552.1741 312.52436 306.65 301.4986 552.1741 301.4986 306.65 301.0044 552.5047 301.0044 306.65 289.97865 552.5047 289.97865 306.65 289.48439 552.55 289.48439 306.65 278.45863 552.55 278.45863 306.65 278.0844 552.2637 278.0844 306.65 267.05867 552.2637 267.05867 306.65 266.5644 552.2238 266.5644 306.65 255.53864 552.2238 255.53864 306.65 255.04438 552.5215 255.04438 306.65 244.01862 552.5215 244.01862 306.65 243.52436 552.2138 243.52436 306.65 232.4986 552.2138 232.4986 306.65 231.97443 552.18399 231.97443 306.65 220.94867 552.18399 220.94867 306.65 220.4544 342.95423 220.4544 306.65 209.42865 342.95423 209.42865]/Rect[304.05113 208.73954 555.14889 336.25349]/AP<</N 375 0 R>>/NM(fitz-A11)/Contents(Passive control: disturbance reduction and gravity gradient stabilization\n\nIn order to stabilize the system, the solar pressure torque affecting the satellite is minimized by using white coatings on the external surface of the satellite. The magnetic torque is also minimized by designing the system with materials that have less impact on the magnetic field used in the system. As a result of the calculations presented in this study, the gravity gradient value is found to be greater than all disturbance forces. Consequently, the system is stabilized with passive forces along the tension in the tether and at a distance equal to the length of the tether from the PocketQube to the CubeSat.)/T(CUBICS camera literature review)/Subj(Passive control: disturbance reduction and gravity gradient stabilization)/BM/Multiply>>
endobj

